 2. 🛡️ Trump vows to protect Elon 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Photos via Getty Images President Trump says he'll try to protect Elon Musk if Democrats investigate the SpaceX and Tesla CEO after tomorrow's midterm elections, Axios' Ben Berkowitz reports. 

 Trump also suggested preemptive pardons for staff and others around him. 🎙️ In an interview for the "Pod Force One" podcast published early today, the New York Post's Miranda Devine asked Trump about rumors of Musk being investigated or having his assets seized.

 Trump said: "It's talk. But if it is talk, we'll have to protect them." 🤑 Musk has spent nearly half a billion dollars opposing Democrats during this election cycle.

 He also recently suggested that it would be the end of democracy if Democrats win the White House and Congress in 2028. Trump also said that he'd consider pardons for his staff and other allies if Democrats pursue them: "I would not even think about it. I'd do it."

