 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Sen. Susan Collins campaigns today at Ellis Family Market in Patten, Maine. Photo: Taylor Coester/Reuters 🗳️ 50 million Americans have already cast ballots in this week's midterm elections. There are some promising signs for Democrats, but it's too early to draw any big conclusions. Explore the data . 🧑‍⚖️ A federal judge dismissed a complaint against two former FBI officials accused of covering up how much they knew about the investigation into a laptop reportedly tied to Hunter Biden. Go deeper . 🌎 Ex-paratrooper Karl Bushby finished his 28-year odyssey of walking around the world today, returning to his mother's home in northern England for the first time since 1998. He told reporters that he depended on "the kindness of strangers, so many, from individuals to nation-states, to get me back here today." Go deeper . Photo: Heidi Gutman/ABC 📺 Sneak peek: Here's a first look at the new ABC News election-night set in Manhattan, where David Muir will anchor at least seven hours of coverage tomorrow across ABC, Disney+, Hulu and ABC News Live, 7 p.m. to 2 a.m. ET. 

 Coverage will include 17 journalists in two new studios, plus 13 correspondents in 11 states from Maine to Alaska. The main set has 150 million pixels across about 6,700 square feet. Preview video . 
 
