 4. 📸 Pic to go: Sign of the times 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: Luiz Rampelotto/EuropaNewswire via Reuters Thousands of friends, family and spectators lined the course of yesterday's New York City Marathon to cheer on the approximately 60,000 runners from more than 140 countries.

 It's one of the best days of the year in the Big Apple, with huge crowds supporting those undertaking the 26.2-mile gauntlet from Staten Island to Central Park via Brooklyn, Queens and the Bronx. 🍿 One popular sign this year: Theranos founder Elizabeth Holmes promising the finish line is near and asking, "Why would I deceive you?" — a reference to the smash hit documentary, "You Can See Everything."

